From: root <root@MyComputer.localdomain>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 13:02:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 32/38] feat(mem_cache): mamba attribution log + audit
 heartbeat + BACKUP-ON-EVICT
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Attribution log: MAMBA-INSERT/MATCH/EVICT/ALLOC-FAIL lines with
branch/boundary/full_kv_hit fields (9-02 diagnosis infrastructure).

Audit heartbeat: DFS every 300s logging nodes/states/deepest/branch_max/
evictable/locked — proved the 9-03 40s full-recompute was cross-session
LRU eviction of an idle session chain during active-period pressure.

BACKUP-ON-EVICT (root-cause fix): evict_component copies a device-only
mamba state to host before freeing its slots (guards skip write-back
BackupKV leaves in flight). Every evicted state keeps a host copy ->
mh=1 LOAD_BACK restore instead of mh=0 tombstone full recompute.
Verified in production 12:45-12:46: eviction+restore same-frame closed
loop, 100% hit rates on returning sessions, zero MAMBA-EVICT-DROP.
